  "description": "Rompope—an eggnog-like combination of milk, egg, spice, and liquor served during the holidays in Mexico—was reportedly created by nuns in the 17th century.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr.\n\nOptional substitutions: aged rum → aguardiente\n\nNotes: Remove the peel of the lemon with a peeler, making sure to avoid the pith. Add rum or aguardiente to taste—and tolerance! I use Flor de Caña 7-year.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Rompope can be refrigerated in sterilized glass bottles for up to 1 month.",
